WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.960
So it has been quite an exciting time for
the elements

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.160
recently. We had element 112 that got its
name

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:14.019
copernecium…oops hang on, we must stop,
I have got the

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:15.599
wrong tie.

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:19.150
So it has been an exciting couple of months
for elements we

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:25.210
had element 112 named copernecium and now
yesterday or

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:30.789
just the end of last week, it was announced
that the synthesis

00:00:30.789 --> 00:00:37.399
of, element 114, had been repeated. It was
made about 10

00:00:37.399 --> 00:00:41.100
years ago in a place called Dubna in Russia,
rather to the

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.879
north of Moscow, it was made like the other
super heavy

00:00:44.879 --> 00:00:51.470
elements, by fusing two nuclei, two atoms
together. So in

00:00:51.470 --> 00:00:57.969
this case they took an atom of plutonium which
has atomic

00:00:57.969 --> 00:01:05.670
number 94, so to get to 114 you need to add
20 to 94, so

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:11.310
they used atoms of calcium which has atomic
number 20 and

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:15.870
electrically-charged atoms of calcium were
accelerated to

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:21.250
huge speed and banged into targets of plutonium.
Now the

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:25.130
people who did the new work which was in Berkeley
in

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:30.310
California had their machine running for 8
days banging away

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:35.721
the calcium atoms into a target of plutonium
oxide and

00:01:35.721 --> 00:01:41.500
managed to observe two atoms of element 114.
Just think for

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.970
a moment, the tiniest grain of dust that you
can see, like the

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:50.830
dust you see on this table, will have hundreds
of thousands of

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:56.100
millions of atoms in it. So if you have one
or two atoms you

00:01:56.100 --> 00:02:00.040
can, not only can you not see it but you can’t
tell anything

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.670
about the properties of the elements or whatever.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:07.800
Now the reason people were trying to make
element 114 is

00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.910
because there have been long standing predictions,
by people

00:02:10.910 --> 00:02:16.450
who do the theory, that perhaps element 114
might be much

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:20.850
more stable than the other elements that have
heavier than

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:24.510
uranium. They imagined, or suggested, that
there would be

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.960
an island of stability, so you would go through
a lot of

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:32.220
elements, 110, 111, 112 that would be very
unstable and

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:35.510
then suddenly you would get to 114 which would
be much

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:40.080
more stable. Unfortunately, it turns out from
the experiments

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.870
that it is not the case. They are only stable
for a fraction of a

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:49.460
second and, like the other heavy elements,
they decay from a

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.830
whole series of different elements, which
themselves can be

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:58.790
detected. So you can see here the decay chain
of element 112

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:03.430
here and borium and a whole series of them
and soon there

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:08.560
will be another decay chain for element 114.
Now the real

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:14.150
importance of this experiment is that the
original work in

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:19.410
Russia has been repeated somewhere else. Now
nobody

00:03:19.410 --> 00:03:23.720
doubted that the Russian experiment was correct
but it is a

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:28.680
general principle of science that nobody believes
an

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:33.140
experiment completely until it has been repeated.
When my

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.960
students do an experiment and get a good result,
I

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:40.040
congratulate them and then I tell them to
do it again just to

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.880
make sure that it works. But of course, just
because the

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.660
same person does the same thing twice they
might be

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:52.190
making the same mistake without realising
it. So if somebody

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.819
else using completely different equipment,
in a completely

00:03:55.819 --> 00:03:59.130
different lab does the same experiment and
gets the same

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:04.430
result then everybody will believe it, and
so this is really quite

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:09.880
an exciting event because now element 114
has been really

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:14.090
quite well established and presumably soon
people will be

00:04:14.090 --> 00:04:18.389
choosing a name and it would be very interesting
to see what

00:04:18.389 --> 00:04:23.800
they choose and at this stage I am not quite
sure what they

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:26.919
might choose but I hope they will be inspired
by the German

00:04:26.919 --> 00:04:31.729
team that named element 112, and name it after
somebody

00:04:31.729 --> 00:04:35.909
who is neither Russian nor American but who
is a famous

00:04:35.909 --> 00:04:38.270
scientist who’s inspired others.

